From: Juan Pablo Lassala <jpablolassala@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 09:37:53 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] background: Draw under Caja's desktop under Camino

On Wayland the plugin makes no background surface while Caja shows the
desktop icons, because both are in the background layer and the
compositor decides which one is on top. Caja's desktop is on one output
only, so every other output had no wallpaper.

Camino, the Wayland compositor for MATE, draws the "desktop" surface above
"mate-background" on the same output. When MATE_WM_NAME is Camino, make
the background surfaces on every output, whatever show-desktop-icons says.
Without that variable, nothing changes.
---
 plugins/background/msd-background-manager-wayland.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/plugins/background/msd-background-manager-wayland.c b/plugins/background/msd-background-manager-wayland.c
index b4ab88d..3b79cfc 100644
--- a/plugins/background/msd-background-manager-wayland.c
+++ b/plugins/background/msd-background-manager-wayland.c
@@ -81,6 +81,13 @@ get_current_time (void)
 static gboolean
 caja_desktop_is_showing (MsdBackgroundManagerWayland *manager)
 {
+	/* Camino, the Wayland compositor for MATE, draws Caja's "desktop"
+	 * surface above "mate-background" on the same output, so the two can
+	 * be there together. Caja has its desktop on one output only: the
+	 * others get their wallpaper from here. */
+	if (g_strcmp0 (g_getenv ("MATE_WM_NAME"), "Camino") == 0)
+		return FALSE;
+
 	return g_settings_get_boolean (manager->settings, MATE_BG_KEY_SHOW_DESKTOP);
 }
 
